Z||000004||theogre||01-14-2000||10:55 PM||||A little known fact is that desputed charges almost always go in the card holders favor. Another even lesser known fact is that there is next to zero way a seller can contest what is called a "charge back."<P>On the other hand you may end up blacklisted by Fiero store. Now when you really need something only they have you won't likely get it.<P>You should have gone to the local parts store <B>in the first place.</B> Fiero store should always be a source of last resort. Same for FOCOA and others. Very few drivetrane and Chasis parts are Fiero only items. The only time things start getting hard to find is when you need body, interior, and a few cooling system parts.<P>In other words I don't feel sorry for people who don't do basic research. You could have just as easily gone to wrenchead.com who even has many things the local chain store says are Dealer Only items.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||01-14-2000||11:01 PM||||I DID check local and no one could get the rebuild kit for a Fiero, but they can get the wagner kit that happens to fit a Fiero. It did not make much sense to me either.||||reg||1
